## How to avoid problems

1. **Test changes in isolation.** When modifying
   {{ title | lower }}, write a targeted test first:
   `pytest -k "{{ feature_name }}"` should catch obvious
   regressions before the change reaches other code.

2. **Watch for implicit state.** Module-level globals,
   cached values, and environment variables can make
   {{ title | lower }} behave differently in tests than in
   production. If a test passes locally but fails in CI,
   suspect implicit state first.

3. **Respect the public API.** Private helpers (names
   starting with `_`) can change without notice. Depend on
   them and you will get surprised during refactors.

